=== Hierarchical Risk Parity (HRP) vs ERC (same panel) ===
cite: López de Prado 2016 JPM 42(4) HRP (title says Outperform OOS — historical title, not a guaranteed Sharpe upgrade)
cite: AFML ch.16 HRP steps — tree clustering, quasi-diagonalization, recursive bisection
dendrogram leaf order: ['C0', 'C1', 'B0', 'B1', 'E0', 'E3', 'E1', 'E2']
ERC RC std=0.000101 (near 0 ⇒ equal risk contributions)
allocation table:
       HRP    ERC  inv_vol
E0  0.1010  0.125   0.1246
E1  0.1019  0.125   0.1290
E2  0.1044  0.125   0.1322
E3  0.1140  0.125   0.1406
B0  0.1382  0.125   0.1149
B1  0.1351  0.125   0.1123
C0  0.1413  0.125   0.1140
C1  0.1641  0.125   0.1324
HRP equity_cluster_sum 0.4214
HRP bond_cluster_sum 0.2733
HRP commodity_cluster_sum 0.3054
ERC equity_cluster_sum 0.5000
teach: inv-vol ignores correlation clusters; ERC equalizes risk contributions; HRP allocates across a hierarchy so a large correlated cluster does not dominate like 1/N-by-ticker
